      "description": "Watch PSV Eindhoven vs AZ Alkmaar highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The Eredivisie clash between PSV Eindhoven and AZ Alkmaar on August 2, 2026, was billed as a high-stakes encounter between two of the league's top contenders. Fans gathered at the stadium expecting a tightly contested battle, but the match would soon be defined by a series of dramatic events that shifted the balance of power early on. A Disastrous Start for the Hosts The tactical plans of PSV Eindhoven were thrown into disarray after just nine minutes. Joey Veerman was shown a straight red card following a serious foul, leaving his side to fight an uphill battle with only ten men. Despite the numerical disadvantage, PSV briefly threatened when Ryan Flamingo connected with a header in the 14th minute, but Jari De Busser produced a comfortable save to keep the scores level. However, the pressure from the visitors eventually told. In the 25th minute, Mexx Meerdink capitalized on a loose ball in the box, reacting quickest to head home and give AZ Alkmaar the lead. The goal allowed the visitors to settle into a rhythm, dominating possession as PSV struggled to cover the gaps left by their missing midfielder. AZ Alkmaar Turn the Screw The second half saw AZ Alkmaar escalate their offensive pressure. In the 51st minute, Peer Koopmeiners turned provider, setting up Weslley Pinto for a composed left-footed finish. The momentum stayed firmly with the visitors, and by the 58th minute, it was 3-0 as Elijah Dijkstra found the net with his right foot following an assist from Ro-Zangelo Daal . The situation went from bad to worse for PSV in the 66th minute. Yarek Gasiorowski tripped Calvin Stengs inside the penalty area, giving the referee no choice but to point to the spot. Ro-Zangelo Daal stepped up and coolly converted the penalty, sending Matej Kovar the wrong way to effectively end the contest as a spectacle. Discipline Fades as the Clock Winds Down As the match entered its final stages, tempers began to flare. The referee was kept busy as Ivan Perisic and Kees Smit both received yellow cards for dissent in the 85th minute, while Ryan Flamingo was also booked late on for a rough challenge. AZ Alkmaar maintained a professional grip on the game, finishing with 65% possession and securing a comprehensive victory that leaves PSV searching for answers after a difficult afternoon."
